    },
    "body": "The native bank reader had no ordinary training loss and the old single-source loss assumed candidates occupied the first contiguous context positions. Add a Rust bank loss that gathers actual causal candidate positions, checks native replay/Q24 parity, and applies one global Copy/Period/Stop alias objective with the existing context/readout credit.\n\nThe source-bound zero-update diagnostic executes all6 development banks/26 canonical targets with positive support and finite recurrent-context/potential/Stop/Period gradients. It reproduces all27 own-prefix steps plus6 initial traces of the prior integer probe; answer quality stays1/6. Existing directed inverse(query)*key H4 geometry is active. Unused content/cross-channel zeros require no binding repair.\n\nValidation:2 library tests,3 example/output tests, release build, cargo fmt --check and claim wording pass; actual LinuxCPU batch exit0. Independent saved audit verifies native alias arithmetic, source bits, BLAKE3 and33 prior traces; Tensor/rawbackward reconstruction remains outside saved-data scope.17-check exact-head review passes. All9 report files902,062B and executable returned with exactSHA/file sets. Complete cost and preserved analysis-only grouping correction are bound in evidence.\n\nNext: counterbalanced banks with different queries over the same sources, retained single-source controls, measured exact broadbatch beforefitadmission. No optimizer update, general chat, longhorizon or M1energy claim. Integer runtime and sharedsession/compiler files unchanged.\n\nReferences #1552. References #820.\n",
